{"id": "EUVD-2026-108295", "enisaUuid": "e01c71c7-8bfb-38c4-b6e9-1d4851235984", "description": "Incus from 7.3.0 before 7.5.0 contains a project restriction bypass that allows restricted project users to set block.create_options through volume update, copy, and move operations. Attackers can set the option on a custom volume and trigger a copy or move onto a formatting pool to inject arguments into mkfs executed as root.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:42", "baseScore": 9.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/lxc/incus/security/advisories/GHSA-4cph-ccqv-hm3c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/incus-7.3.0-before-7.5.0-project-restriction-bypass-via-block-create-options"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9cgf-rjhv-pjh5", "CVE-2026-115372"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d28722f7-11e3-3a80-a60a-c893a12000bf", "product": {"name": "incus", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}, "product_version": "7.3.0 <7.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "37de7b5a-f980-3570-9422-64a935166007", "vendor": {"name": "lxc"}}], "isExploited": false}